  "steps": [
    "<strong>Roast the Tofu:</strong> Heat oven to 200°C / 400°F. Tear pressed tofu into chunky pieces.",
    "Toss tofu with oil, smoked paprika, garam masala, salt, and pepper. Spread on a lined tray and bake 30–35 minutes, flipping once, until deeply golden and firm.",
    "<strong>Make the Sauce:</strong> Heat oil or butter in a pan over medium heat. Add onion and cook about 10 minutes until very soft and lightly caramelised.",
    "Add garlic and ginger; cook 1 minute. Stir in garam masala, coriander, chilli powder, and tomato purée.",
    "Add chopped tomatoes and simmer 10 minutes until thick and rich. Stir in cream or cashew cream and season with salt and lemon juice.",
    "Fold roasted tofu into the sauce just before serving to keep it slightly crisp."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Tearing tofu instead of cubing gives better texture and sauce cling.",
    "Cashew cream keeps it fully vegan and extra luxurious.",
    "Add tofu at the end so it stays roasted, not spongey."
  ]
